{"term":"conclude","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:350aefd530e71d92dd","definition":"To end; to come to an end.","example":"The story concluded with a moral.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["begin","initiate","start","commence"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["concludable","concluder","concludible","conclusible","inconcludability","misconclude","reconclude","unconcluded"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/conclude#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:04935053b6531ecbe9","definition":"To bring to an end; to close; to finish.","example":"I will conclude this part with the speech of a counsellor of state.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["begin","initiate","start","commence"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["concludable","concluder","concludible","conclusible","inconcludability","misconclude","reconclude","unconcluded"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/conclude#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:b0b5f5d0b8844b9242","definition":"To bring about as a result; to effect; to make.","example":"to conclude a bargain","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["begin","initiate","start","commence"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["concludable","concluder","concludible","conclusible","inconcludability","misconclude","reconclude","unconcluded"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/conclude#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:db5e88da1c6719d35e","definition":"To come to a conclusion, to a final decision.","example":"From the evidence, I conclude that this man was murdered.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["begin","initiate","start","commence"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["concludable","concluder","concludible","conclusible","inconcludability","misconclude","reconclude","unconcluded"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/conclude#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:4b92b20227ff2fc530","definition":"To make a final determination or judgment concerning; to judge; to decide.","example":"But no frail man, however great or high, / Can be concluded blest before he die.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["begin","initiate","start","commence"],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete","wordFamily":["concludable","concluder","concludible","conclusible","inconcludability","misconclude","reconclude","unconcluded"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/conclude#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:8b99be7dd14a429b67","definition":"To shut off; to restrain; to limit; to estop; to bar.","example":"The defendant is concluded by his own plea.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["begin","initiate","start","commence"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["concludable","concluder","concludible","conclusible","inconcludability","misconclude","reconclude","unconcluded"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/conclude#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:9c8ff0ddf6254e9371","definition":"To shut up; to enclose.","example":"The very person of Christ [was] concluded within the grave.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["begin","initiate","start","commence"],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete","wordFamily":["concludable","concluder","concludible","conclusible","inconcludability","misconclude","reconclude","unconcluded"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/conclude#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:138d38b0168b9810fc","definition":"To include; to comprehend; to shut up together; to embrace; to confine.","example":"Banisht the Court? Let me be banisht Life;\n Since the chief end of Life is there concluded:\nWithin the Court is all the Kingdom bounded,\nAnd as her sacred Sphear doth comprehend\nTen thousand times so much, as so much Place\nIn any part of all the Empire else;\nSo every Body, moving in her Sphear,\nContains Ten thousand times as much in him,\nAs any other, her choice Orb excludes.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["begin","initiate","start","commence"],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete","wordFamily":["concludable","concluder","concludible","conclusible","inconcludability","misconclude","reconclude","unconcluded"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/conclude#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:f6ea2fbd3b28ce14b2","definition":"to deduce, to infer (develop a causal relation)","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["begin","initiate","start","commence"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["concludable","concluder","concludible","conclusible","inconcludability","misconclude","reconclude","unconcluded"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/conclude#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"}],"pronunciation":{"ipa":"/kənˈkluːd/","us":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/2/24/En-us-conclude.ogg/En-us-conclude.ogg.mp3"},"wordFamily":["concludable","concluder","concludible","conclusible","inconcludability","misconclude","reconclude","unconcluded"]}